 "published": false,
 "title": "A private Japanese candle-making experience in Kamakura.",
 "description": "<p style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:#57646f;margin-top:0.5em;margin-bottom:0.5em\">Zenrise designs slow, considered private experiences around Kamakura and its surrounding towns. A private wa-rōsoku(Japanese candle) making session with Meria, a wax artist based in Shonan, arranged for up to four guests at a time, in a quiet space in Kamakura or Fujisawa. Every candle begins as a wick, dipped again and again into molten wax until it takes shape — entirely by hand. Natural materials from local farmers and growers — the character of Shonan, held in a single flame. The finished candle is yours to take home, a keepsake you&#39;ll return to each time you light it.</p>",
 "excerpt": "Experience a private Japanese candle-making session with wax artist Meria, from Shonan Wa-Rōsoku. Held in Kamakura or Fujisawa.",
